id: pm-0682l4
title: "GH-827: local package install must prevent recursive self-copy and disk exhaustion"
description: "Installing a local package whose tracker and extension destination are inside the source recursively copies the destination and backups into themselves, including node_modules, while reporting success."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags[5]: "area:packages",data-safety,github-intake,reliability,security
created_at: "2026-07-30T11:28:35.807Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T11:28:35.807Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Install rejects or safely prunes destination-inside-source; tracker roots, backups, and node_modules cannot enter installed copies; repeated-install acceptance proves bounded size; failures never report ok true"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make the normal local package development install loop bounded and containment-safe
value: Package authors cannot exhaust disks by repeatedly installing their own checkout
impact: Prevents exponential storage growth and ENOSPC failures in standard package layouts
parent: pm-doxj
